1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,395
One missing part can interrupt a favorite
routine.

2
00:00:03,515 --> 00:00:06,910
Meanwhile, useful electronics sit in
drawers because we

3
00:00:07,030 --> 00:00:10,001
don't know what to do with them.

4
00:00:10,121 --> 00:00:13,940
Orphan Parts Lens starts with two
questions: what do

5
00:00:14,060 --> 00:00:17,880
you have, and what do you want to
accomplish?

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,545
I use this older Hamilton Beach drink
mixer to make frappé coffee.

7
00:00:23,665 --> 00:00:26,437
Finding a replacement mixing component
means

8
00:00:26,557 --> 00:00:28,867
understanding more than its appearance.

9
00:00:28,987 --> 00:00:33,146
I photograph the appliance, its label, and
the component.

10
00:00:33,266 --> 00:00:38,810
The app helps identify what information is
missing and what needs checking.

11
00:00:38,930 --> 00:00:44,013
It starts with a replacement part; a donor
appliance, or another

12
00:00:44,133 --> 00:00:49,215
device that produces the result I want, is
the next step.

13
00:00:49,335 --> 00:00:54,880
The useful answer includes the evidence
and questions needed before I buy.

14
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,005
The same approach applies to my unused
electronics.

15
00:00:59,125 --> 00:01:03,130
I catalog my laptops, monitors, tablets,
and accessories.

16
00:01:03,250 --> 00:01:07,755
Then I explain my interests, budget, and
experience, so

17
00:01:07,875 --> 00:01:11,880
the suggestions fit both my equipment and
me.

18
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:18,192
Perhaps I want a home automation server, a
smart mirror, or a tabletop arcade.

19
00:01:18,312 --> 00:01:20,081
I choose the arcade.

20
00:01:20,201 --> 00:01:23,739
The plan identifies which existing
components could be

21
00:01:23,859 --> 00:01:27,397
reused, what needs testing, and what is
missing.

22
00:01:27,517 --> 00:01:31,940
Marketplace becomes a starting point for
finding those missing pieces

23
00:01:32,060 --> 00:01:36,483
locally: the app opens the search, and I
run it.

24
00:01:36,603 --> 00:01:41,910
The build pack collects the items, the
steps, and the safety notes.

25
00:01:42,030 --> 00:01:46,895
A connection diagram and an assembly
preview, shown here as concept

26
00:01:47,015 --> 00:01:51,880
previews, would explain how the computer,
display, and controls work together.

27
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:56,073
The next step is a plan that adapts.

28
00:01:56,193 --> 00:02:00,265
If I choose a different display, the app

29
00:02:00,385 --> 00:02:04,458
should reconsider the connections,
enclosure dimensions, and instructions.

30
00:02:04,578 --> 00:02:09,669
That is the direction shown in this
concept preview: a

31
00:02:09,789 --> 00:02:14,880
downloadable build package, including
designs for suitable brackets or housings.

32
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:19,047
This would be useful because it connects a

33
00:02:19,167 --> 00:02:22,707
practical goal with things people already
own.

34
00:02:22,828 --> 00:02:27,380
It could help avoid unsuitable purchases,
uncover worthwhile reuse

35
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:31,547
projects, and make secondhand parts easier
to evaluate.

36
00:02:31,667 --> 00:02:35,713
Each confirmed result could also become
useful evidence

37
00:02:35,833 --> 00:02:39,880
for the next person facing the same
problem.

38
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,856
Orphan Parts Lens.

39
00:02:42,976 --> 00:02:44,880
Find replacements.

40
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,904
Discover reuse.

41
00:02:47,024 --> 00:02:49,880
Build something useful.

